<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="eedc5589">The baseline contains current financial data and the structure of annual operating expenditures of the organizational
units in scope for the current state analysis and any other useful operational information. It also factors in assumptions
such as data pertaining to growth rate/inflation, and potential impact of additional on-going/planned projects.</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="ffb27902"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="7309c31d">Completion of the Financial and Operational Performance Baseline is likely to require data from across a range of
departments and systems within the organization.</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="f6d2a206"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="d1951a1a">To capture the existing operating costs and current state performance data prior to the introduction of any change in the
organization.</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="adfcd949"></attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="ff61b151"></attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="17fe5ea1"></attribute>
<attribute name="representationOptions" nodeId="19f1f734">The Financial and Operational Performance Baseline is typically maintained as a spreadsheet.</attribute>
